  "content": {
    "id": "p141-q32-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "32",
    "prompt": "Find the domain and range of $y=\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Domain: $[0,1]$; range: $[0,1]$.",
      "worked": "The inner square root requires $x\\ge0$. The outer square root requires\n$$\\begin{align*}1-\\sqrt{x}&\\ge0\\\\\\sqrt{x}&\\le1\\\\x&\\le1.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth restrictions must hold, so the domain is $[0,1]$.\n\nAt $x=0$, $y=1$; at $x=1$, $y=0$. As $x$ increases through $[0,1]$, $\\sqrt{x}$ increases continuously, so $\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}$ decreases continuously from $1$ to $0$.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[0,1]$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
